cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this board design in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "mouse-joystick-pcb: single-axis mouse joystick controller board"
abstract: >-
  KiCad design, fabrication outputs and documentation for a single-axis mouse
  joystick controller PCB used as a native pyControl peripheral in the Janelia
  Dudman lab joystick rig: an RP2040, a TMC5130A stepper driver with encoder
  and limit-switch inputs, a brake current sink, a torque bridge, analog angle
  and torque outputs, and a 50-pin digital instrument port.
authors:
